<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n71072" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νοστ-έω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>go</i> or <i>come home, return,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ν. ἐς πατρίδα γαῖαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					1.290
				</span></i>
			, Epic. ap. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.297b
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ν. οἴκαδε, οἶκόνδε, ὅνδε
				δόμονδε,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				4.103
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				5.687
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				1.83
			</span></i>: c. acc., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ν. Ἄργος, οἶκον,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OC</u>
				1386
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>IT</u>
				534
			</span></i>: pleon., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀπίσω ν.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					3.26
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ν. πάλιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Av.</u>
					1270
				</span></i>
			: c. dat. modi, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ν. κεινῇσι χερσί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					1.73
				</span></i>
			:—
				Med.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νοστήσατο πάτρην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Q.S.
					1.269
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> abs.,
				<i>return safe,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				10.247
			</span></i>; <i>return,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἢ εὖ ἦε κακῶς νοστήσομεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					2.253
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάλλιον ἂν . . ἐνόστησ᾽ ἀντιπάλων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>N.</u>
					11.26
				</span></i>
			, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>go</i> or <i>come,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κεῖσε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					4.619
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δεῦρο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Hel.</u>
					474
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γῆν τήνδε</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				891
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰς ἐκκλησίαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Ach.</u>
				</span></i>
			
			
			<i><span class="en">
				29
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b> c. acc.
			cogn., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπὸ γῆς νοστήσαντι πορείαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Ep.</u>
					335c
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νόστος</span> II, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νόστιμος</span> II) <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνόστησε τὸ
				ὕδωρ</span> the water <i>became drinkable,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Paus.
				7.2.11
			</span></i>.</div>
